Security audit (module: rate-limit):
  Threat model: a hostile client wants to exhaust the per-IP bucket
  for ONE victim by spamming requests with their IP forged via
  X-Forwarded-For, OR drown the LRU map itself with millions of
  distinct keys.

  - X-Forwarded-For is only honoured when TRUST_PROXY=true (set at
    boot, default false). clientIp() falls back to req.socket.remote
    when untrusted. Verified at backend/src/index.ts:66 + lib/rate-
    limit.ts:clientIp.
  - Bucket map uses a fixed window (windowMs). Entry is replaced
    rather than reset, so a new window starts fresh — no DoS via
    "keep the bucket pinned at 1 forever".
  - No LRU eviction on the bucket map. POTENTIAL ISSUE: a flood of
    unique IPs (botnet) could grow the map unboundedly until
    next-window prune. Bun's V8 string interning + 60s windows
    bound this in practice (entries auto-prune as their window
    expires on next touch), but a 10M-key spike would still pin
    memory for ~60s. Acceptable for a self-hosted single-tenant
    shop; if a customer hits this, switch to a TTL-aware LRU.
    Flagged for v1.2 polish list rather than blocking v1.1.

  No active vulns found. Map-growth pattern noted for future tuning.

